    "summary": "Thunder‑charged Looks Like Rain and classic Scarlet>Fire sequence",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a thunder‑charged Looks Like Rain and an inspired Scarlet Begonias → Fire On the Mountain → Estimated Prophet → Eyes Of the World suite. Jerry’s guitar is on fire while Brent provides lush keyboards throughout. A solid first set rounds out the performance.",
    "review": "May 15, 1981 at Rutgers University's Athletic Center captures the Dead in top form. The first set crackles with energy—Mississippi Half‑Step Uptown Toodeloo rolls into a seamless Franklin's Tower, and Candyman leads into a bluesy Little Red Rooster before the crowd is swept up by Ramble On Rose and a thunder‑charged Looks Like Rain that had the house howling. \n\nThe second set is the highlight: a flawless Scarlet Begonias → Fire On The Mountain → Estimated Prophet → Eyes Of The World sequence that showcases Jerry’s powerful, soaring guitar tone, Brent’s rich, fully integrated keyboards, and Bob’s impassioned “don’t give up the fight” line during the Prophet. The rhythm section stays tight throughout, closing with a joyous U.S. Blues encore.",
